# ── Dart / pub ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.dart_tool/
.packages
pubspec_overrides.yaml
build/

# ── Deploy tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.wrangler/

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real credentials are supplied at build/deploy time via env vars — see
# each package's build.sh / deploy.sh. Only the *.example templates are
# tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRIVATE PROJECT MATERIAL
#
# This repository is public. Everything below would expose commercial
# strategy, an unreleased roadmap, or a security posture, so it stays
# local.
#
# NOTE THE LEADING SLASHES — they anchor each rule to the repository
# ROOT. Without one, `docs/` would also match kola_server/docs/, which
# holds every SQL migration. Silently dropping the schema history out of
# version control is the kind of thing nobody notices until they need to
# rebuild a database.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Ignore the whole docs folder, then allow back the few files that are
# genuinely meant to be public. Deny-by-default: a new strategy document
# dropped in here is private automatically, rather than public until
# someone remembers to add a rule.
/docs/*

# ── Allowed back: published and user-facing only ─────────────────────────
# Legal documents that are (or will be) published on the website. Having
# them in the repo is a feature, not a leak.
!/docs/PRIVACY_POLICY.md
!/docs/TERMS_OF_SERVICE.md
# A setup walkthrough written FOR customers. Same content as the docs
# site; nothing internal in it.
!/docs/WHATSAPP_MANUAL_SETUP.md

# WHAT STAYS PRIVATE, AND WHY — for whoever reads this later:
#   DEVELOPMENT_PLAN, RELEASE_PHASES  — the unreleased roadmap, in full
#   BUILD_AUDIT_*                     — enumerates known gaps and
#                                       weaknesses. Reconnaissance if
#                                       read by the wrong person
#   ADMIN_APP_SPEC, DESIGN_BRIEF_ADMIN— the admin security boundary,
#                                       permission levels, and what is
#                                       enforced where
#   DESIGN_BRIEF_*, *_DESIGN_PROMPT   — unbuilt UI, positioning, pricing
#   PRD, SRS, COMPETITIVE_FEATURES    — product spec and competitive
#                                       analysis
#   STRATEGY_ALIGNMENT_CHECK          — commercial strategy
#   META_CONNECT_FLOW                 — integration approach research
#   *.docx                            — the same material, exported

# ── Design source ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Design-tool exports of unreleased screens. The built Jaspr apps are the
# real deliverable; these would publish the whole product's UI before it
# ships.
/Kola design system specs/
/Kola design system specs.zip
/screenshots/

# ── Scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/future_consideration.txt

# ── OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
